# Build safety

- Every stop carries a `BuildIssue` (kind, spot, block or item, attempts), saved in `BuildProgress` and sent to the owner's client; `WorkPage` shows its `what()` and `fix()`. `UNLOADED`, `PLACE_FAILED` and `ERROR` are temporary until they repeat `BuildIssue.REPEATED` times at the same step; the others need the player, so `SessionBuild.begin` runs `FarmBuilder.check` before resuming and stays stopped with "Still blocked" when the cause is still there. A chunk that takes over 5 seconds becomes an `UNLOADED` issue without stopping. Never stop a build without a `BuildIssue`.
- In `FarmBuilder`, a step runs in this order: check everything (chunk loaded, already built, protected obstacle, material available, via `blocker`), place, confirm the block is there, and only then spend the material, record the step and advance. Obstacle drops run after a confirmed placement (`ObstacleRules.afterReplace`). A step that stops at any point leaves the counts untouched, so retrying never spends twice or drops twice.
- "Already built" and "still the table's block" use `BlockMatch` (direction, half, axis, bed part, door hinge, rotation, mounting face, slab type, liquid level). Don't compare block types only, and don't compare state that changes on its own, such as open doors, power, shape, or connections.
- A new build is refused unless every step fits the world height and border (`FarmBuilder.fits`). Unexpected errors in a step pause the build, never the server.
- Each build stores `FarmTemplate.signature()`. A build whose farm file changed can't be resumed, and Discard leaves its blocks in place, because its saved step numbers would point at other steps.
- Place, clear and dismantle with `Block.NOTIFY_LISTENERS | Block.FORCE_STATE`, never with neighbor updates. `settle()` runs one update pass when the farm is finished.
- Never clear protected blocks: block entities, unbreakable blocks, redstone parts, pistons, rails, TNT, infested blocks, and anything in `ObstacleRules.KEEP`. Add new exceptions there.
- Record every step the table places with `recordPlaced(usedItem)`.
- Use `FarmSite` for every world position of a farm (`target`, `footprint`, `fits`); never mutate a session to test a spot. `TableSession.problemAt` is the single check for whether a farm can start somewhere, used by Build and by the hologram check.
- Every started build reserves its area in `FarmAreas` (one per world, all tables); every dismantle job has a key that includes its own site, so simultaneous jobs from one table never replace each other's reservation; a finished build is recorded as a `FINISHED` area that outlives the session and the table. New farms can't overlap any area (`conflict`), builds never clear blocks inside another one. Build areas are released on discard, farm change and table break; dismantle areas when that exact job ends; finished areas only when `conflict` finds less than half of their blocks standing.
- Builds and dismantle jobs only work while their player is online, and keep their chunks loaded through `ChunkKeeper` (table radius 1, spot radius 0, tickets expire after 100 ticks without renewal).
- Never look up a finished farm's design by its farm id: use `FarmAreas.Finished.layout()`, so an update that changes or removes a farm can't break its repairs or take-aparts. Each persisted layout has its own saved id (`LayoutId`), even when its legacy signature matches another layout with different block-entity NBT.
- A repair (`SessionBuild.beginRepair`, `BuildProgress.repair`) never clears a block: a spot holding another solid block is skipped and counted as kept when it isn't `stillFarm`. `FarmAreas.presence` splits spots into farm, missing (replaceable) and changed (`FarmAreas.spot`) and totals the items missing spots need. Entity steps are matched by their own block position. A minecart pair is complete only with exactly one correct passenger mounted in exactly one vanilla cart; one free passenger or one empty cart may be completed, while occupied or ambiguous combinations stop with `ENTITY_BLOCKED`. A failed attempt discards only entities it created.
- Server-side jobs never crash the tick: a `FarmDismantler` that throws is dropped with a chat message and a log entry; `FarmLoader` logs a failure once until it works again. Builds and take-aparts that waited for their offline player say so when they continue.
- Hand items to players only through `Handover`: what doesn't fit drops at their feet, and the player is told once per operation.
- `FarmCare` repairs (a new build of the same farm, site, facing and swaps after releasing its `FINISHED` area, re-recorded if the build is refused) and takes down (a `FarmDismantler` over every step) finished farms from My Farms. Repair preserves the finished farm's immutable `instanceId`, custom name, grants, and pending invites across refusal, completion, and restart; a legacy in-progress Repair without an identity receives one on load. Repair, Take Down and Forget cross the network in `FarmCarePayload` with the farm's stable key; never encode a mutable list index for these actions. The server resolves the key again for the acting owner and permits Forget only when the saved layout is unavailable. `FarmStorage` gives a finished farm's status (unloaded, running, full) from its chests and barrels.
- Plant segments on the same plant (`FarmGrowth`: sugar cane, bamboo, cactus, kelp) are growth: never placed, never asked for as material, never counted missing. Only the plant's lowest block is part of the build.
- `FarmLoader` also gives picked farms' chunks random ticks itself when no player is within 128 blocks (the game won't), and resets the idle timeout of their dimension; `ChunkKeeper.keepTable` resets it for running builds.
- `FarmLoader` (overworld persistent state) keeps selected `FINISHED` areas by immutable `dimension|instanceId`, migrating legacy `dimension|table/spot` keys only after every world loads. Reducing the quota never deletes valid selections above it; only the first selections up to the current quota load, and only keys for truly missing farms are pruned. Tickets renew every 100 ticks and load only while the applicable online rule is satisfied. The authorized list reaches a client only through `LoadedFarmsPayload`. Natural mob spawning still needs a player within 128 blocks.
- Never clear blocks in `#the_dream_table:protected`. Creative builds run at `DreamTableConfig.maxBlocksPerSecond()`; every rate respects it.
- Pace lives in `BuildPace`: a share of `DreamTableConfig.maxBlocksPerSecond()` from 1% to 100%, stored as `1000 + percent` (`ofPercent`, `percent`). Slow, Normal, Fast are 25, 50, 100 (default Normal); the Custom slider sends `BUTTON_PACE_CUSTOM + percent` only on release. Old minute saves (-10, -5, -1) map to Slow, Normal, Fast; anything else becomes the default. The Options cards show the real time for the chosen farm. `BuildProgress.due` spreads the rate over ticks. `FarmBuilder.placeNext` returns `PLACED`, `SKIPPED` (block already in place, doesn't use the pace) or `STOPPED`.
- A delivery that supplies the step a build is waiting on continues the build (`TableSession.offerFromHand`).
- Creative deliveries are counted in the ledger's `free` counts: used first, never mark a step as paid, never refunded, never return a water bucket.
- Discard hands the unfinished build to a `FarmDismantler` job ticked by the table (32 blocks per tick, saved under `Dismantling`) and frees the session at once.
- Taking apart and counting missing blocks use `BlockMatch.stillFarm` (also accepts farmland turned dirt, bamboo grown from its shoot). After each batch, `FarmDismantler.settle` sends neighbor and shape updates so cane, crops, torches, redstone and piston heads left without support drop.
- Discard only takes apart unfinished builds, and only steps the table placed that still match with `BlockMatch.sameShape`, so a block the player turned or replaced stays. Refunds go only to paid steps. Water refunds nothing, because the bucket came back when it was poured. Empty containers into the player's hands before removing them.
- Material counts are always keyed by the template's original item. `resolve()` gives the swapped item.
- A material can be swapped only before any of it is delivered and before the build starts.
- Respect protected land through `BuildPermission`: a new build needs `canBuildAll` for the starter; each step checks the online owner (`canBreak` for obstacles, `canPlace` otherwise) and stops with a `PROTECTED` issue; Discard skips blocks the discarding player can't break. Never place or remove blocks around these checks.
- Keep NBT key names stable so existing worlds keep loading. New data gets new keys with safe defaults.
